    "body": "### Problem\n\ndiscussed in https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/41387 \n\nThe ability to annotate mappings (`vim.keymap.set()`) and user commands `nvim_create_user_command` with a \"namespace\":\n\n- https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/32261#issuecomment-2626858431\n- https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/992#issuecomment-2577779050\n\n... is relevant for `CmdAtom` events, which are naturally scoped to a mapping or Ex command.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nWhen a CmdAtom event is emitted, it should include a `CmdAtom.namespace` field based on the associated mapping or command that produced the CmdAtom.\n\n\n### Other ideas\n\nUse-cases for plugin-defined \"actions\" (fictional `setrepeat()` or `declare_action()` which annotates the current action):\n\n- replay/repeat a mapping that interacts with terminal-mode (`:FzfLua files`). currently not possible bc Nvim cannot know when the action \"ends\" (there is no count-verb-noun-etc grammar).\n    - plugins like fzf-lua could declare when the action ends, and how to repeat it.",
